{
  "//": "rust-analyzer defaults to `cargo check --all-targets`, which builds the test target. The `test` crate does not exist for bare-metal targets (nor for the esp-idf build-std set), so without these Zed reports `E0463: can't find crate for test` on a project that builds fine. See rust-analyzer.toml in the project root for the full rationale. Zed passes `initialization_options` straight through as the server's LSP initialization options, which is the delivery path that actually suppresses this diagnostic; note Zed requires NESTED objects here and does not accept VS Code's dotted key style.",
  "lsp": {
    "rust-analyzer": {
      "initialization_options": {
        "cargo": {
          "allTargets": false
        },
        "check": {
          "allTargets": false
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
